#: ../../provisioning/jobs/security_scan.rst:2
msgid "Creating and Running Security Scan Jobs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../provisioning/jobs/security_scan.rst:4
msgid ""
"Security Scan Jobs allow users to create and schedule SCAP program "
"(Security Content Automation Program) scans for groups of managed "
"systems. These Jobs can call in existing SCAP packages and checklists, "
"which are used to scan the targeted systems on-demand or on a scheduled "
"basis. Historical data for these scans is saved in the Job Execution list"
" and in the software section of server detail pages. Detailed scan "
"reports can also be viewed for each system as needed once the scan is "
"complete. See the `SCAP documentation "
"<https://csrc.nist.gov/CSRC/media/Projects/Security-Content-Automation-"
"Protocol/documents/docs/scap-nistir-7343.pdf>`_ on the NIST website for "
"information on developing your own scanning procedures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../provisioning/jobs/security_scan.rst:6
#: ../../provisioning/jobs/security_scan.rst:11
msgid "Note"
msgstr ""

#: ../../provisioning/jobs/security_scan.rst:6
msgid ""
"Creating and editing Security Scan Jobs requires the \"Security: "
"Scanning\" Role permission set to Full. Viewing Security Scan Jobs and "
"seeing the results for scanned servers requires at least a Read-level "
"permission."
msgstr ""

